{
  "_id": "fhSubCmbtCock001",
  "name": "Combat Cocktail",
  "type": "consumable",
  "img": "icons/svg/item-bag.svg",
  "folder": "fhSubSciFi000001",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A pre-loaded auto-injector blending battlefield analgesics with off-label muscle accelerators. Issued unofficially to private military contractors; recovered routinely from the dead. The label warns of cardiac risk in fine print no one reads.</p><p><strong><em>Desired effects on use.</em></strong> For 1 minute you gain a +2 bonus to weapon attack rolls and damage rolls.</p><p><strong><em>On use, save against addiction.</em></strong> Make a DC 14 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, you gain the Addicted condition from Combat Cocktail (see below).</p><p><strong><em>Addicted from Combat Cocktail.</em></strong> While you have this Addicted condition, you are also Poisoned and have disadvantage on Charisma saving throws (you can't shake the post-firefight jitter).</p><p><strong><em>Withdrawal.</em></strong> At the end of each Long Rest while addicted, you either take another dose or abstain. If you abstain, make a DC 12 Wisdom check to resist the craving; on a failure, you give in and take a dose. On a success, you go into withdrawal for 3 days, or half that if you succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw. If you have no doses left, skip the Wisdom check. While in withdrawal all your speeds are reduced by 10 feet, you have disadvantage on Strength and Constitution saving throws, and in combat you take 1d4 poison damage at the start of each of your turns. Abstaining then takes only the Wisdom check, and taking any dose ends the withdrawal but not the addiction. When the withdrawal ends, so does the addiction.</p><p><strong><em>Overdose.</em></strong> If you take a dose while still under its effects, or once your tolerance is at its limit, there is a 10% chance you overdose: you take 2d8 poison damage and have the Poisoned and Incapacitated conditions for 1 minute.</p><p><strong><em>Dosing others.</em></strong> As an action, you can fire a dart at a creature within 20 feet, making a ranged attack. On a hit, the creature is dosed.</p><p><em>Requires ready paraphernalia that applies to injury substances, such as a Jet Injector or a Neural Shunt.</em></p>"
    },
